# Commit Conventions

Format: `<type>(<scope>): <subject>`

## Types

| Type | When |
|------|------|
| `feat` | New feature visible to users or API consumers |
| `fix` | Bug fix |
| `perf` | Performance improvement |
| `refactor` | Code restructuring without behaviour change |
| `test` | Tests added or corrected |
| `docs` | Documentation only |
| `chore` | Build, deps, tooling, config (no production code) |
| `style` | Formatting/whitespace only (no logic change) |
| `a11y` | Accessibility improvement |
| `ci` | CI/CD pipeline |

## Scopes (optional but recommended)

- `web` – Angular frontend (`apps/web/`)
- `api` – Express backend (`apps/api/`)
- `e2e` – Playwright tests (`apps/e2e/`)
- `a11y` – Accessibility changes
- `deps` – Dependency updates
- `hooks` – `.cursor/hooks/` changes
- `rules` – `.cursor/rules/` changes

## Subject Rules

- Imperative mood: "add", "fix", "remove" – not "added", "fixes"
- Lowercase, no period at end
- Max 72 characters
- Body optional: explain *why*, not *what*

## Examples

```
feat(web): add keyboard shortcut to refresh versions list
fix(api): prevent shell injection via alias name input
perf(api): replace nvm ls with direct fs.readdir scan
refactor(web): extract version-badge to standalone component
test(api): add supertest coverage for POST /versions/use
a11y(web): add aria-live region to installed-versions-card
docs: update CHANGELOG for v1.3.0
chore(deps): update @angular/* to 21.3.0
```

## What NOT to do

```
// ❌
git commit -m "fix stuff"
git commit -m "WIP"
git commit -m "Update"
git commit -m "Fixed the bug in the component"
```
